This configuration adds a modest position dependence to the left and right actions (‑1·position for left, +1·position for right) while keeping the strong velocity‑driven selection and a large negative bias for the no‑acceleration action. The added position term should encourage the car to accelerate left when it is far left and right when it is far right, potentially reducing the number of steps needed to reach the goal compared to the pure velocity‑only policy.
